/* Verse Games: THE WHOLE COUNSEL · Exodus chapters 31-35
   Verse text is filled/verified from the KJV by tools/fill-verses.js */
VG.registerBibleChapters("exodus", [
{n:31, name:"Bezalel and the Sabbath", seal:{ref:"Exodus 31:18",verse:"And he gave unto Moses, when he had made an end of communing with him upon mount Sinai, two tables of testimony, tables of stone, written with the finger of God."}, facts:["Did you know Bezalel is the first person in Scripture described as filled with the spirit of God for craftsmanship? The Spirit's filling was for building, not just for speaking.","Did you know the Sabbath command comes right before the golden calf chapters? The sign of the covenant was given just before Israel broke it.","Did you know Exodus 31:18 is the first mention of the tables of stone, written with the finger of God? No human hand touched the writing."], questions:[
{q:"Whom did the LORD call by name to lead the work of the tabernacle?",options:["Bezalel the son of Uri, of the tribe of Judah","Aholiab the son of Ahisamach, of the tribe of Dan","Moses the son of Amram, of the tribe of Levi","Hur the prince of Judah"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 31:2",verse:"See, I have called by name Bezaleel the son of Uri, the son of Hur, of the tribe of Judah:",insight:"God called Bezalel by name before He described his task. God knows your name too, and His calling always comes before His assignment."},
{q:"With what did God fill Bezalel for the work?",options:["The spirit of God, in wisdom, and in understanding, and in knowledge, and in all manner of workmanship","The gold of the treasury of Egypt","The strength of ten mighty men","The tongues of the wise and learned"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 31:3",verse:"And I have filled him with the spirit of God, in wisdom, and in understanding, and in knowledge, and in all manner of workmanship,",insight:"The first person filled with the Spirit in Scripture was a craftsman, not a preacher. The Holy Spirit cares about skilled work done for God."},
{q:"How many gifts are listed as filling Bezalel in Exodus 31:3?",options:["Four: wisdom, understanding, knowledge, and all manner of workmanship","Three: faith, hope, and charity","Seven: the seven spirits of God","Two: strength and skill"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 31:3",verse:"And I have filled him with the spirit of God, in wisdom, and in understanding, and in knowledge, and in all manner of workmanship,",insight:"God gave Bezalel a complete set of gifts for the work. He equips fully for what He asks, never leaving the work half supplied."},
{q:"In which three metals was Bezalel to devise cunning works?",options:["Gold, silver, and brass","Gold, silver, and iron","Brass, copper, and tin","Silver, iron, and lead"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 31:4",verse:"To devise cunning works, to work in gold, and in silver, and in brass,",insight:"The most precious metals were shaped for God's house by Spirit-filled hands. What you make with excellence can carry His glory."},
{q:"Besides metalwork, which two crafts did the workmen practice?",options:["Cutting of stones and carving of timber","Weaving of silk and dyeing of wool","Building of altars and digging of wells","Casting of bells and forging of swords"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 31:5",verse:"And in cutting of stones, to set them, and in carving of timber, to work in all manner of workmanship.",insight:"Stone and timber, hard materials, yielded to Spirit-given skill. No work is too rough or plain for God to fill with His Spirit."},
{q:"Who did God give to work alongside Bezalel?",options:["Aholiab the son of Ahisamach, of the tribe of Dan","Oholiab the son of Caleb, of Benjamin","Eliab the son of Helon, of Zebulun","Ahinoam the son of Jether, of Issachar"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 31:6",verse:"And I, behold, I have given with him Aholiab, the son of Ahisamach, of the tribe of Dan: and in the hearts of all that are wise hearted I have put wisdom, that they may make all that I have commanded thee;",insight:"God gave Bezalel a partner, not a rival. Kingdom work is shared work; He pairs us so the load is carried together."},
{q:"What did God put in the hearts of all the wise hearted?",options:["Wisdom","Riches","Strength","Long life"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 31:6",verse:"And I, behold, I have given with him Aholiab, the son of Ahisamach, of the tribe of Dan: and in the hearts of all that are wise hearted I have put wisdom, that they may make all that I have commanded thee;",insight:"Wisdom was God's gift placed inside the craftsmen. If you lack wisdom for your task, He is the Giver to ask."},
{q:"What was the chief structure the wise hearted were to make?",options:["The tabernacle of the congregation","A temple of stone in Jerusalem","A tower reaching to heaven","A palace for Moses"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 31:7",verse:"The tabernacle of the congregation, and the ark of the testimony, and the mercy seat that is thereupon, and all the furniture of the tabernacle,",insight:"The tabernacle was a meeting place, God's address among His people. God builds so He can dwell near you."},
{q:"Which holy furniture stood within the vail of the tabernacle?",options:["The ark of the testimony with the mercy seat above it","The table of shewbread","The golden candlestick","The altar of burnt offering"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 31:7",verse:"The tabernacle of the congregation, and the ark of the testimony, and the mercy seat that is thereupon, and all the furniture of the tabernacle,",insight:"The ark held God's testimony at the heart of the tabernacle. At the center of your life, keep His word enthroned."},
{q:"For whom were the holy garments to be made?",options:["For Aaron and his sons, for the priest's office","For Moses and the elders of Israel","For Bezalel and Aholiab the craftsmen","For the princes of the tribes"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 31:10",verse:"And the cloths of service, and the holy garments for Aaron the priest, and the garments of his sons, to minister in the priest’s office,",insight:"The priests' garments were holy because the service was holy. What you bring to meet God matters, but more so the heart beneath it."},
{q:"What was Sabbath keeping to be between God and Israel?",options:["A sign between me and you throughout your generations","A secret known only to the priests","A tax paid to the tabernacle","A song sung every morning"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 31:13",verse:"Speak thou also unto the children of Israel, saying, Verily my sabbaths ye shall keep: for it is a sign between me and you throughout your generations; that ye may know that I am the LORD that doth sanctify you.",insight:"The Sabbath was a visible sign of an invisible covenant. Your rest in God is a testimony others can see."},
{q:"What would keeping the Sabbath teach Israel to know?",options:["That I am the LORD that doth sanctify you","That Moses was greater than Pharaoh","That Egypt had been left forever","That the tabernacle was finished"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 31:13",verse:"Speak thou also unto the children of Israel, saying, Verily my sabbaths ye shall keep: for it is a sign between me and you throughout your generations; that ye may know that I am the LORD that doth sanctify you.",insight:"Rest taught Israel who sanctified them: the LORD, not their labor. You are made holy by Him, not by your striving."},
{q:"What was the penalty for defiling the Sabbath?",options:["He shall surely be put to death","He shall pay a double offering","He shall be exiled for a year","He shall fast for seven days"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 31:14",verse:"Ye shall keep the sabbath therefore; for it is holy unto you: every one that defileth it shall surely be put to death: for whosoever doeth any work therein, that soul shall be cut off from among his people.",insight:"The sentence is severe because the sign is sacred. Treating God's holy things lightly has always carried weight."},
{q:"How is the weekly rhythm described in Exodus 31:15?",options:["Six days may work be done, but the seventh is the sabbath of rest","Seven days of work, then a feast day","Five days of work and two days of rest","Work until the task is done, then rest"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 31:15",verse:"Six days may work be done; but in the seventh is the sabbath of rest, holy to the LORD: whosoever doeth any work in the sabbath day, he shall surely be put to death.",insight:"Six days of work, one of rest: God's rhythm protects us from ourselves. Workaholism is not devotion; it breaks His design."},
{q:"What kind of covenant was the Sabbath to be?",options:["A perpetual covenant","A covenant for one generation","A covenant only for the priests","A covenant until the tabernacle was built"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 31:16",verse:"Wherefore the children of Israel shall keep the sabbath, to observe the sabbath throughout their generations, for a perpetual covenant.",insight:"Perpetual means the Sabbath was not a passing rule. God's rest is woven into time itself, forever."},
{q:"Between whom was the Sabbath a sign forever?",options:["Between God and the children of Israel","Between Moses and Aaron","Between Judah and Dan","Between the priests and the people"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 31:17",verse:"It is a sign between me and the children of Israel for ever: for in six days the LORD made heaven and earth, and on the seventh day he rested, and was refreshed.",insight:"The sign marked Israel as God's own, forever. Resting in Him still marks who belongs to Him."},
{q:"What did the LORD do on the seventh day, according to Exodus 31:17?",options:["He rested, and was refreshed","He judged the nations","He counted the stars","He called the prophets"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 31:17",verse:"It is a sign between me and the children of Israel for ever: for in six days the LORD made heaven and earth, and on the seventh day he rested, and was refreshed.",insight:"Scripture says God was refreshed by rest, not from weariness but from delight. Rest refreshes because it is God's own pattern."},
{q:"To whom did the LORD speak concerning the workmen of the tabernacle?",options:["Moses","Aaron","Bezalel","Joshua"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 31:1",verse:"And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,",insight:"Every detail of the tabernacle came by direct revelation to Moses. True worship follows God's pattern, not man's invention."},
{q:"With what were the tables of testimony written?",options:["With the finger of God","With the pen of Moses","With the chisel of Bezalel","With the quill of Aaron"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 31:18",verse:"And he gave unto Moses, when he had made an end of communing with him upon mount Sinai, two tables of testimony, tables of stone, written with the finger of God.",insight:"The finger of God means no human hand shaped those words. Scripture's authority rests on its divine Author."},
{q:"Which two sacred items were prepared for the service of the sanctuary?",options:["The anointing oil and sweet incense","The shewbread and the drink offering","The ephod and the breastplate","The laver and the mercy seat"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 31:11",verse:"And the anointing oil, and sweet incense for the holy place: according to all that I have commanded thee shall they do.",insight:"Oil for consecration and incense for prayer belonged in the holy place. Dedication and prayer still belong at the heart of worship."}
]},
{n:32, name:"The Golden Calf", seal:{ref:"Exodus 32:26",verse:"Then Moses stood in the gate of the camp, and said, Who is on the LORD’S side? let him come unto me. And all the sons of Levi gathered themselves together unto him."}, facts:["Did you know Aaron blamed the fire itself? 'I cast it into the fire, and there came out this calf' is Scripture's picture of refusing to own our sin.","Did you know about three thousand fell at Sinai, while about three thousand were added to the church at Pentecost? The letter kills, but the Spirit gives life.","Did you know Moses broke the tables at the foot of the mount? The shattered stones pictured the covenant Israel had already shattered."], questions:[
{q:"What did the people demand of Aaron when Moses delayed on the mount?",options:["Up, make us gods, which shall go before us","Build us a tower to reach the heavens","Give us a king like the nations","Take us back to Egypt"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 32:1",verse:"And when the people saw that Moses delayed to come down out of the mount, the people gathered themselves together unto Aaron, and said unto him, Up, make us gods, which shall go before us; for as for this Moses, the man that brought us up out of the land of Egypt, we wot not what is become of him.",insight:"They wanted a god they could see, right now. Impatience with God's timing still tempts us to manufacture our own answers."},
{q:"Why did the people turn to Aaron?",options:["They did not know what had become of Moses","Moses had commanded them to wait forever","Aaron had promised them gold","The Egyptians were pursuing them"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 32:1",verse:"And when the people saw that Moses delayed to come down out of the mount, the people gathered themselves together unto Aaron, and said unto him, Up, make us gods, which shall go before us; for as for this Moses, the man that brought us up out of the land of Egypt, we wot not what is become of him.",insight:"'We wot not what is become of him' was their excuse for idolatry. Uncertainty about God's servant never justifies abandoning God."},
{q:"What did Aaron ask the people to bring him?",options:["The golden earrings from their ears","Silver coins from their purses","Bronze vessels from their tents","Purple cloth from their looms"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 32:2",verse:"And Aaron said unto them, Break off the golden earrings, which are in the ears of your wives, of your sons, and of your daughters, and bring them unto me.",insight:"The gold of Egypt, once plundered by God's deliverance, was melted into an idol. Blessings misused become bondage."},
{q:"With what tool did Aaron fashion the golden calf?",options:["A graving tool","A hammer and anvil","A furnace and bellows","A chisel and mallet"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 32:4",verse:"And he received them at their hand, and fashioned it with a graving tool, after he had made it a molten calf: and they said, These be thy gods, O Israel, which brought thee up out of the land of Egypt.",insight:"Idolatry took skilled craftsmanship, the very skill God had given for the tabernacle. Gifts meant for God can be twisted into gods."},
{q:"What did the people cry over the calf?",options:["These be thy gods, O Israel, which brought thee up out of the land of Egypt","Behold the god of Moses who speaks from the mount","This is the LORD who goes before us","Glory to the calf that saved us"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 32:4",verse:"And he received them at their hand, and fashioned it with a graving tool, after he had made it a molten calf: and they said, These be thy gods, O Israel, which brought thee up out of the land of Egypt.",insight:"They credited the calf with the Exodus. False worship always rewrites history, stealing God's works for something else."},
{q:"What did Aaron proclaim for the next day?",options:["To morrow is a feast to the LORD","To morrow we return to Egypt","To morrow Moses will descend","To morrow the calf will speak"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 32:5",verse:"And when Aaron saw it, he built an altar before it; and Aaron made proclamation, and said, To morrow is a feast to the LORD.",insight:"Aaron dressed idolatry in the LORD's name. Mixing true religion with false worship does not sanctify it; it corrupts it."},
{q:"What did the people do after they ate and drank before the calf?",options:["They rose up to play","They fell down to pray","They went up to sacrifice","They sat down to mourn"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 32:6",verse:"And they rose up early on the morrow, and offered burnt offerings, and brought peace offerings; and the people sat down to eat and to drink, and rose up to play.",insight:"Play here meant revelry, not innocence. Worship that ends in self-indulgence was never worship at all."},
{q:"What did God call Israel in Exodus 32:9?",options:["A stiffnecked people","A faithless generation","A rebellious house","A wayward flock"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 32:9",verse:"And the LORD said unto Moses, I have seen this people, and, behold, it is a stiffnecked people:",insight:"Stiffnecked pictures an ox that will not turn. God names the sin plainly: a neck that refuses to bend to Him."},
{q:"What did God propose to do with Israel, and with Moses?",options:["Consume them, and make of Moses a great nation","Scatter them among the nations","Send them back to Egypt","Strike them with pestilence alone"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 32:10",verse:"Now therefore let me alone, that my wrath may wax hot against them, and that I may consume them: and I will make of thee a great nation.",insight:"God offered Moses a fresh start without Israel. True intercession refuses a blessing that costs the people."},
{q:"Whom did Moses remind God of in his intercession?",options:["Abraham, Isaac, and Israel, to whom God swore by Himself","Noah, Shem, and Japheth","Joseph and his brothers","Adam and his sons"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 32:13",verse:"Remember Abraham, Isaac, and Israel, thy servants, to whom thou swarest by thine own self, and saidst unto them, I will multiply your seed as the stars of heaven, and all this land that I have spoken of will I give unto your seed, and they shall inherit it for ever.",insight:"Moses pleaded God's own promises, not Israel's worthiness. Prayer has power when it stands on what God has sworn."},
{q:"What did the LORD do in response to Moses' prayer?",options:["He repented of the evil He thought to do to His people","He struck the camp with fire","He withdrew His presence forever","He hardened Pharaoh's heart"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 32:14",verse:"And the LORD repented of the evil which he thought to do unto his people.",insight:"Repented means God turned from the judgment, moved by intercession. One man's prayer can turn aside wrath."},
{q:"What did Joshua think he heard in the camp?",options:["The noise of war","The sound of trumpets","The singing of Moses","The roar of thunder"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 32:17",verse:"And when Joshua heard the noise of the people as they shouted, he said unto Moses, There is a noise of war in the camp.",insight:"Joshua heard noise but could not name it. From a distance, sin's revelry can sound like battle; up close, it is shame."},
{q:"What did Moses say the noise really was?",options:["The noise of them that sing","The cry of the wounded","The shout of victory","The wailing of mourners"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 32:18",verse:"And he said, It is not the voice of them that shout for mastery, neither is it the voice of them that cry for being overcome: but the noise of them that sing do I hear.",insight:"Moses discerned what Joshua could not: celebration around a calf. Discernment tells the difference between worship and noise."},
{q:"What did Moses do with the tables of stone when he saw the calf?",options:["He cast them from his hands and broke them beneath the mount","He hid them in his tent","He threw them into the fire","He gave them to Aaron"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 32:19",verse:"And it came to pass, as soon as he came nigh unto the camp, that he saw the calf, and the dancing: and Moses’ anger waxed hot, and he cast the tables out of his hands, and brake them beneath the mount.",insight:"The broken tables pictured the broken covenant. Moses did not smash them in a tantrum; he enacted what Israel had done."},
{q:"What did Moses do to the golden calf?",options:["He burned it, ground it to powder, and scattered it on the water","He buried it under the mount","He gave it to the Levites","He melted it into a crown"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 32:20",verse:"And he took the calf which they had made, and burnt it in the fire, and ground it to powder, and strawed it upon the water, and made the children of Israel drink of it.",insight:"The god they worshiped became dust in their drink. Every idol, faced honestly, dissolves into nothing."},
{q:"What were the children of Israel made to drink?",options:["The powdered calf scattered on the water","Bitter water from Marah","Wine left from the feast","Water from the rock"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 32:20",verse:"And he took the calf which they had made, and burnt it in the fire, and ground it to powder, and strawed it upon the water, and made the children of Israel drink of it.",insight:"They had to swallow their idol. Sin consumed becomes bitterness; God made them taste what they had chosen."},
{q:"What was Aaron's excuse for the calf?",options:["I cast the gold into the fire, and there came out this calf","The people forced my hand with threats","Moses delayed and I panicked","The Egyptians taught me this craft"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 32:24",verse:"And I said unto them, Whosoever hath any gold, let them break it off. So they gave it me: then I cast it into the fire, and there came out this calf.",insight:"Aaron blamed the fire, as if the calf made itself. Excuses that erase our choices never erase our guilt."},
{q:"What was Moses' rallying cry to the camp?",options:["Who is on the LORD's side? let him come unto me","Who will follow me to the promised land","Who will stand against the Egyptians","Who will build the tabernacle"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 32:26",verse:"Then Moses stood in the gate of the camp, and said, Who is on the LORD’S side? let him come unto me. And all the sons of Levi gathered themselves together unto him.",insight:"Neutrality ended with that question. In every crisis of faith, the LORD's side is the only side worth choosing."},
{q:"About how many men fell that day by the sword of the Levites?",options:["About three thousand","About six hundred","About ten thousand","About seventy"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 32:28",verse:"And the children of Levi did according to the word of Moses: and there fell of the people that day about three thousand men.",insight:"Three thousand died for the calf on the day the law came down. Judgment for sin is real, and Scripture does not soften the number."},
{q:"What did Moses ask God to do to him if Israel could not be forgiven?",options:["Blot me out of Thy book which Thou hast written","Cast me out from the camp","Take my life with the sword","Remove my name from the tribes"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 32:32",verse:"Yet now, if thou wilt forgive their sin, and if not, blot me, I pray thee, out of thy book which thou hast written.",insight:"Moses offered himself in Israel's place, a shadow of Christ. Love that intercedes is willing to be spent."}
]},
{n:33, name:"Moses Intercedes", seal:{ref:"Exodus 33:14",verse:"And he said, My presence shall go with thee, and I will give thee rest."}, facts:["Did you know Moses pitched the tent of meeting outside the camp? Anyone who sought the LORD had to walk out to find Him.","Did you know 'face to face' describes friendship, not appearance? Moses still could not see God's face and live.","Did you know Joshua stayed behind in the tabernacle when Moses left? Lingering in God's presence was his training to lead."], questions:[
{q:"To which land did the LORD tell Moses to lead the people?",options:["The land He swore to Abraham, to Isaac, and to Jacob","The land of Goshen in Egypt","The wilderness of Paran","The plains of Moab"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 33:1",verse:"And the LORD said unto Moses, Depart, and go up hence, thou and the people which thou hast brought up out of the land of Egypt, unto the land which I sware unto Abraham, to Isaac, and to Jacob, saying, Unto thy seed will I give it:",insight:"The promise still stood, sworn to the patriarchs. God's oath outlasts Israel's failure; His word does not break when we do."},
{q:"Whom would God send before Israel into the land?",options:["An angel","A pillar of fire by night","The ark carried by priests","Joshua with the captains"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 33:2",verse:"And I will send an angel before thee; and I will drive out the Canaanite, the Amorite, and the Hittite, and the Perizzite, the Hivite, and the Jebusite:",insight:"An angel would go, but God's own presence would not. Lesser blessings still go with us, but they are no substitute for Him."},
{q:"Why would God not go up in the midst of Israel?",options:["They were a stiffnecked people, and He might consume them in the way","The ark of the covenant was not yet finished","Moses had not yet returned from the mount","The Canaanites were too strong to face"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 33:3",verse:"Unto a land flowing with milk and honey: for I will not go up in the midst of thee; for thou art a stiffnecked people: lest I consume thee in the way.",insight:"God's holiness and their stubbornness could not travel together. Sin makes God's nearness dangerous, which is why we need a Mediator."},
{q:"How did the people respond to these evil tidings?",options:["They mourned, and no man put on his ornaments","They rejoiced and held a feast","They blamed Moses aloud","They packed to return to Egypt"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 33:4",verse:"And when the people heard these evil tidings, they mourned: and no man did put on him his ornaments.",insight:"They mourned the threatened loss of God's presence. Sometimes we only learn what we had when we hear it may be withdrawn."},
{q:"What did the LORD command the people to put off?",options:["Their ornaments","Their sandals","Their weapons","Their veils"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 33:5",verse:"For the LORD had said unto Moses, Say unto the children of Israel, Ye are a stiffnecked people: I will come up into the midst of thee in a moment, and consume thee: therefore now put off thy ornaments from thee, that I may know what to do unto thee.",insight:"Ornaments came off as a sign of mourning. Stripping away decoration was their first step back toward God."},
{q:"Where did Moses pitch the tabernacle of meeting?",options:["Without the camp, afar off from the camp","In the midst of the camp","On the top of Mount Sinai","Beside the shore of the Red Sea"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 33:7",verse:"And Moses took the tabernacle, and pitched it without the camp, afar off from the camp, and called it the Tabernacle of the congregation. And it came to pass, that every one which sought the LORD went out unto the tabernacle of the congregation, which was without the camp.",insight:"The tent moved outside the camp because the camp had defiled itself. God was still reachable, but no longer casually near."},
{q:"What was this tent called?",options:["The Tabernacle of the congregation","The Tent of the Testimony","The House of Prayer","The Pavilion of Peace"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 33:7",verse:"And Moses took the tabernacle, and pitched it without the camp, afar off from the camp, and called it the Tabernacle of the congregation. And it came to pass, that every one which sought the LORD went out unto the tabernacle of the congregation, which was without the camp.",insight:"Congregation means those who gather to Him. God names the meeting place after the seekers, not the structure."},
{q:"What did all the people do when Moses went out to the tabernacle?",options:["They stood and looked after him until he entered","They followed him into the tent","They turned back to their work","They sang as he passed by"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 33:8",verse:"And it came to pass, when Moses went out unto the tabernacle, that all the people rose up, and stood every man at his tent door, and looked after Moses, until he was gone into the tabernacle.",insight:"The whole camp watched one man go to meet God. A praying life is never private; others are watching your walk."},
{q:"What descended and stood at the door of the tabernacle?",options:["The cloudy pillar","A flame of fire","A rushing wind","A bright star"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 33:9",verse:"And it came to pass, as Moses entered into the tabernacle, the cloudy pillar descended, and stood at the door of the tabernacle, and the LORD talked with Moses.",insight:"The pillar that had led them now waited at the tent door. God's guidance pauses where prayer begins."},
{q:"What did the people do when they saw the cloudy pillar?",options:["They worshipped, every man in his tent door","They drew near to touch it","They covered their faces and fled","They offered burnt sacrifices"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 33:10",verse:"And all the people saw the cloudy pillar stand at the tabernacle door: and all the people rose up and worshipped, every man in his tent door.",insight:"They worshiped from a distance, each at his own door. Reverence keeps its distance; awe does not presume."},
{q:"How did the LORD speak to Moses?",options:["Face to face, as a man speaketh unto his friend","Through dreams in the night","By the voice of thunder only","Through the high priest's ephod"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 33:11",verse:"And the LORD spake unto Moses face to face, as a man speaketh unto his friend. And he turned again into the camp: but his servant Joshua, the son of Nun, a young man, departed not out of the tabernacle.",insight:"As a man speaketh unto his friend is Scripture's highest picture of prayer. God invites friendship, not just formal worship."},
{q:"Who did not depart out of the tabernacle?",options:["Joshua the son of Nun, Moses' servant","Aaron the priest","Hur the elder","Eleazar the scribe"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 33:11",verse:"And the LORD spake unto Moses face to face, as a man speaketh unto his friend. And he turned again into the camp: but his servant Joshua, the son of Nun, a young man, departed not out of the tabernacle.",insight:"Joshua lingered in God's presence after Moses left. Those who stay when others go are being prepared to lead."},
{q:"What did Moses ask God to show him?",options:["Thy way, that I may know Thee","The tablets of the law","The route through the wilderness","The face of Pharaoh"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 33:13",verse:"Now therefore, I pray thee, if I have found grace in thy sight, shew me now thy way, that I may know thee, that I may find grace in thy sight: and consider that this nation is thy people.",insight:"Moses asked for God's way, not just God's help. Knowing God's path matters more than getting God's power."},
{q:"What did the LORD promise Moses?",options:["My presence shall go with thee, and I will give thee rest","I will make thee a great nation","I will send thee back to Egypt","I will give thee the land alone"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 33:14",verse:"And he said, My presence shall go with thee, and I will give thee rest.",insight:"Presence and rest: God's twofold gift. With Him beside you, the wilderness itself becomes a resting place."},
{q:"What did Moses say if God's presence did not go with them?",options:["Carry us not up hence","We will go in our own strength","Send the angel instead","We will wait forty years"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 33:15",verse:"And he said unto him, If thy presence go not with me, carry us not up hence.",insight:"Moses would rather stay in the wilderness with God than enter Canaan without Him. The land is nothing; the Lord is everything."},
{q:"How would Israel be known to have found grace?",options:["In that God went with them, separating them from all people","By the gold they carried from Egypt","By the number of their fighting men","By the height of their tabernacle"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 33:16",verse:"For wherein shall it be known here that I and thy people have found grace in thy sight? is it not in that thou goest with us? so shall we be separated, I and thy people, from all the people that are upon the face of the earth.",insight:"What marked Israel was not army or wealth but God's company. The church is distinguished the same way: by His presence."},
{q:"What bold request did Moses make in Exodus 33:18?",options:["I beseech Thee, shew me Thy glory","Give me the land of Canaan","Let me see the promised rest","Make my face to shine"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 33:18",verse:"And he said, I beseech thee, shew me thy glory.",insight:"After forgiveness came hunger for more of God. Grace received should make us ask for glory, not grow content."},
{q:"What did God promise to make pass before Moses?",options:["All His goodness","All His judgments","All His angels","All His mighty works"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 33:19",verse:"And he said, I will make all my goodness pass before thee, and I will proclaim the name of the LORD before thee; and will be gracious to whom I will be gracious, and will shew mercy on whom I will shew mercy.",insight:"God answered 'shew me Thy glory' with 'all My goodness.' His glory is His goodness; to know Him is to know He is good."},
{q:"Why could Moses not see God's face?",options:["No man shall see God and live","The cloud was too thick","Moses had sinned at the calf","The glory had already passed"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 33:20",verse:"And he said, Thou canst not see my face: for there shall no man see me, and live.",insight:"Even the friend of God could not bear the full blaze of His face. Holiness is not harshness; it is brightness too strong for us."},
{q:"What would Moses see as God's glory passed by?",options:["His back parts, from the cleft of the rock","His face in the cloud","His hand upon the mount","His feet upon the altar"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 33:23",verse:"And I will take away mine hand, and thou shalt see my back parts: but my face shall not be seen.",insight:"God covered Moses with His hand and let him see what followed. We see God best in hindsight: His faithfulness behind us."}
]},
{n:34, name:"The Shining Face", seal:{ref:"Exodus 34:6",verse:"And the LORD passed by before him, and proclaimed, The LORD, The LORD God, merciful and gracious, longsuffering, and abundant in goodness and truth,"}, facts:["Did you know the words of Exodus 34:6-7 echo through the rest of the Old Testament? David, Nehemiah, and Jonah all quote God's self-description.","Did you know Moses did not know his face was shining? Closeness to God shows on us before we notice it ourselves.","Did you know God names Himself 'Jealous'? His jealousy guards the covenant the way a husband guards a marriage."], questions:[
{q:"What did Moses hew at God's command?",options:["Two tables of stone like unto the first","Two tablets of gold for the ark","Two pillars for the tabernacle door","Two stones for the altar"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 34:1",verse:"And the LORD said unto Moses, Hew thee two tables of stone like unto the first: and I will write upon these tables the words that were in the first tables, which thou brakest.",insight:"Moses cut the new stones; God would write the words. We prepare the tablets of our hearts; He writes His law on them."},
{q:"What would God write on the new tables?",options:["The words that were in the first tables, which thou brakest","A new and different covenant","The names of the twelve tribes","The song of Moses"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 34:1",verse:"And the LORD said unto Moses, Hew thee two tables of stone like unto the first: and I will write upon these tables the words that were in the first tables, which thou brakest.",insight:"God restored exactly what was broken, word for word. His covenant survives our failures; grace rewrites what sin shattered."},
{q:"When was Moses to present himself on the mount?",options:["Be ready in the morning, and come up to the top of the mount","At midnight under the stars","At the setting of the sun","On the seventh day"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 34:2",verse:"And be ready in the morning, and come up in the morning unto mount Sinai, and present thyself there to me in the top of the mount.",insight:"Morning was the appointed time. Meeting God first, before the day's demands, was Moses' pattern too."},
{q:"What did the LORD do when He descended in the cloud?",options:["He stood with Moses and proclaimed the name of the LORD","He wrote on the tables at once","He called the elders to ascend","He covered the mount with fire"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 34:5",verse:"And the LORD descended in the cloud, and stood with him there, and proclaimed the name of the LORD.",insight:"God proclaimed His own name, His character. He wants to be known; revelation is His idea, not ours."},
{q:"How did God describe Himself in Exodus 34:6?",options:["Merciful and gracious, longsuffering, and abundant in goodness and truth","Mighty and terrible in judgment","Holy and unapproachable in light","Silent and hidden from men"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 34:6",verse:"And the LORD passed by before him, and proclaimed, The LORD, The LORD God, merciful and gracious, longsuffering, and abundant in goodness and truth,",insight:"Mercy comes first in God's self-portrait. Before He is anything else to sinners, He is merciful and gracious."},
{q:"What does God keep for thousands?",options:["Mercy, forgiving iniquity and transgression and sin","Wrath for the rebellious","Records of every deed","Silence toward the proud"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 34:7",verse:"Keeping mercy for thousands, forgiving iniquity and transgression and sin, and that will by no means clear the guilty; visiting the iniquity of the fathers upon the children, and upon the children’s children, unto the third and to the fourth generation.",insight:"Keeping mercy for thousands means His mercy is stored up, not spent. Generations draw from it, and it never runs dry."},
{q:"What did Moses do when he heard God's name proclaimed?",options:["He made haste, and bowed his head toward the earth, and worshipped","He covered his face with the vail","He called for Aaron to ascend","He wrote the words in a book"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 34:8",verse:"And Moses made haste, and bowed his head toward the earth, and worshipped.",insight:"The revelation of God's mercy drove Moses to his knees. True worship is the heart's answer to who God is."},
{q:"What did God promise to do before all the people?",options:["Do marvels such as have not been done in all the earth","Give them rest from all their enemies","Build them a city with walls","Send rain in its season"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 34:10",verse:"And he said, Behold, I make a covenant: before all thy people I will do marvels, such as have not been done in all the earth, nor in any nation: and all the people among which thou art shall see the work of the LORD: for it is a terrible thing that I will do with thee.",insight:"Marvels would mark the covenant people. God's wonders were not entertainment; they were credentials of His presence."},
{q:"Which six nations would God drive out before Israel?",options:["The Amorite, Canaanite, Hittite, Perizzite, Hivite, and Jebusite","The Egyptian, Assyrian, Babylonian, Persian, Greek, and Roman","The Moabite, Ammonite, Edomite, Philistine, Amalekite, and Midianite","The Kenite, Kenizzite, Kadmonite, Rephaim, Girgashite, and Horite"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 34:11",verse:"Observe thou that which I command thee this day: behold, I drive out before thee the Amorite, and the Canaanite, and the Hittite, and the Perizzite, and the Hivite, and the Jebusite.",insight:"God named the enemies He would remove. He fights the battles He assigns; our part is to observe what He commands."},
{q:"What were the Israelites warned not to do with the land's inhabitants?",options:["Make a covenant with them, lest it become a snare","Trade with them at the gates","Learn their languages","Marry their widows"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 34:12",verse:"Take heed to thyself, lest thou make a covenant with the inhabitants of the land whither thou goest, lest it be for a snare in the midst of thee:",insight:"A snare is hidden until it springs. Compromise with what God forbids always looks harmless at first."},
{q:"What were they to do to the altars, images, and groves?",options:["Destroy their altars, break their images, and cut down their groves","Leave them standing as warnings","Dedicate them to the LORD","Sell them for silver"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 34:13",verse:"But ye shall destroy their altars, break their images, and cut down their groves:",insight:"Idolatry was to be demolished, not managed. Half measures with sin leave the snare standing."},
{q:"Why were they to worship no other god?",options:["The LORD, whose name is Jealous, is a jealous God","The other gods were made of wood","Moses had commanded it alone","The priests would lose their office"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 34:14",verse:"For thou shalt worship no other god: for the LORD, whose name is Jealous, is a jealous God:",insight:"God calls Himself Jealous by name. His jealousy is covenant love refusing to share the heart He redeemed."},
{q:"What kind of gods were forbidden in Exodus 34:17?",options:["Molten gods","Gods of silver only","Gods made by strangers","Gods of the Egyptians"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 34:17",verse:"Thou shalt make thee no molten gods.",insight:"No molten gods struck at the calf all over again. The command targeted Israel's exact weakness."},
{q:"How long was Moses on the mount the second time?",options:["Forty days and forty nights","Seven days and seven nights","Three days and three nights","Twelve days and twelve nights"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 34:28",verse:"And he was there with the LORD forty days and forty nights; he did neither eat bread, nor drink water. And he wrote upon the tables the words of the covenant, the ten commandments.",insight:"Forty days, twice. God's law was worth two months on the mountain. Some gifts only come to those who stay."},
{q:"What was written on the tables this second time?",options:["The words of the covenant, the ten commandments","The names of the tribes of Israel","The song of deliverance","The judgments of the law"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 34:28",verse:"And he was there with the LORD forty days and forty nights; he did neither eat bread, nor drink water. And he wrote upon the tables the words of the covenant, the ten commandments.",insight:"The ten commandments were written again, unchanged. God's standards do not shift because we broke them."},
{q:"What happened to the skin of Moses' face when he came down?",options:["It shone","It was burned","It was pale","It was marked"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 34:29",verse:"And it came to pass, when Moses came down from mount Sinai with the two tables of testimony in Moses’ hand, when he came down from the mount, that Moses wist not that the skin of his face shone while he talked with him.",insight:"Forty days with God left a glow Moses could not hide. Time with the Lord leaves a mark that words cannot fake."},
{q:"How did Aaron and the people react to Moses' shining face?",options:["They were afraid to come nigh him","They fell down and worshipped him","They asked him to remove the glow","They covered their own faces"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 34:30",verse:"And when Aaron and all the children of Israel saw Moses, behold, the skin of his face shone; and they were afraid to come nigh him.",insight:"Glory frightens the guilty conscience. The same light that comforts the clean convicts the compromised."},
{q:"What did Moses put on his face?",options:["A vail","A crown of gold","A linen cloth","An ephod"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 34:33",verse:"And till Moses had done speaking with them, he put a vail on his face.",insight:"The veil softened the glory for fearful eyes. God lets His servants veil the brightness when people cannot bear it."},
{q:"When did Moses take the vail off?",options:["When he went in before the LORD to speak with Him","When he ate with the elders","When he entered the camp at night","When he slept in his tent"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 34:34",verse:"But when Moses went in before the LORD to speak with him, he took the vail off, until he came out. And he came out, and spake unto the children of Israel that which he was commanded.",insight:"Unveiled before God, veiled before men: the pattern of every minister. Open with the Lord, measured with the people."},
{q:"What did the children of Israel see whenever Moses came out?",options:["That the skin of his face shone","That his garments were torn","That his staff had budded","That his hair had turned white"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 34:35",verse:"And the children of Israel saw the face of Moses, that the skin of Moses’ face shone: and Moses put the vail upon his face again, until he went in to speak with him.",insight:"The people kept seeing the shine, again and again. A life that keeps meeting God keeps showing it."}
]},
{n:35, name:"The Call to Build", seal:{ref:"Exodus 35:35",verse:"Them hath he filled with wisdom of heart, to work all manner of work, of the engraver, and of the cunning workman, and of the embroiderer, in blue, and in purple, in scarlet, and in fine linen, and of the weaver, even of them that do any work, and of those that devise cunning work."}, facts:["Did you know the Sabbath command is repeated before the building begins? Worship comes before work; rest frames the labor.","Did you know every gift for the tabernacle was voluntary? Nothing was demanded by tax; only what willing hearts brought.","Did you know Bezalel was given the gift of teaching? God put it in his heart 'that he may teach,' so the skill would multiply in others."], questions:[
{q:"Whom did Moses gather to hear the LORD's words?",options:["All the congregation of the children of Israel","The elders and the priests only","The tribe of Judah alone","The men of war"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 35:1",verse:"And Moses gathered all the congregation of the children of Israel together, and said unto them, These are the words which the LORD hath commanded, that ye should do them.",insight:"The whole congregation heard the call, not just the leaders. God's work belongs to all His people, not a chosen few."},
{q:"How many days was work to be done, and what was the seventh day?",options:["Six days of work, but the seventh an holy day, a sabbath of rest","Five days of work, and the sixth and seventh for feasting","Seven days of work, then rest when finished","Work every day except the new moon"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 35:2",verse:"Six days shall work be done, but on the seventh day there shall be to you an holy day, a sabbath of rest to the LORD: whosoever doeth work therein shall be put to death.",insight:"Even tabernacle work, holy work, stopped for the Sabbath. No work is so sacred that it excuses breaking God's rest."},
{q:"What was the penalty for doing work on the Sabbath?",options:["He shall be put to death","He shall pay a double offering","He shall be exiled for a year","He shall fast for seven days"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 35:2",verse:"Six days shall work be done, but on the seventh day there shall be to you an holy day, a sabbath of rest to the LORD: whosoever doeth work therein shall be put to death.",insight:"The sentence is severe because the sign is sacred. Treating God's holy things lightly has always carried weight."},
{q:"What was forbidden throughout their habitations on the Sabbath?",options:["To kindle any fire","To cook any food","To draw any water","To speak any word"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 35:3",verse:"Ye shall kindle no fire throughout your habitations upon the sabbath day.",insight:"No fire meant no work started the day. God wanted rest so complete that not even a spark of labor was lit."},
{q:"Whose heart was invited to bring the offering?",options:["Whosoever is of a willing heart","Every firstborn son","The rich among the tribes","The elders by command"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 35:5",verse:"Take ye from among you an offering unto the LORD: whosoever is of a willing heart, let him bring it, an offering of the LORD; gold, and silver, and brass,",insight:"Willing heart is the only qualification. God wants givers, not taxes; joy, not compulsion."},
{q:"Which three metals were brought for the offering?",options:["Gold, silver, and brass","Gold, silver, and iron","Copper, tin, and lead","Silver, brass, and iron"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 35:5",verse:"Take ye from among you an offering unto the LORD: whosoever is of a willing heart, let him bring it, an offering of the LORD; gold, and silver, and brass,",insight:"The wealth of Egypt, once their chains, became God's house. What God redeems, He repurposes."},
{q:"Which colors of thread were offered?",options:["Blue, purple, and scarlet, with fine linen","Red, yellow, and green, with coarse wool","Blue and white, with sackcloth","Purple and gold, with silk"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 35:6",verse:"And blue, and purple, and scarlet, and fine linen, and goats’ hair,",insight:"Rich colors for a glorious dwelling. Beauty in worship is not waste; it honors the One being worshiped."},
{q:"What skins were brought for the coverings?",options:["Rams' skins dyed red, and badgers' skins","Goats' skins and calves' skins","Lions' skins and bears' skins","Sheepskins white as snow"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 35:7",verse:"And rams’ skins dyed red, and badgers’ skins, and shittim wood,",insight:"Humble animal skins covered the glory within. God often wraps His greatest treasures in plain coverings."},
{q:"What wood was offered for the building?",options:["Shittim wood","Cedar of Lebanon","Olive wood","Cypress from the hills"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 35:7",verse:"And rams’ skins dyed red, and badgers’ skins, and shittim wood,",insight:"Shittim wood, desert acacia, tough and lasting. God builds with what grows in the wilderness, not just what is imported."},
{q:"What were the oil and spices for?",options:["Oil for the light, and spices for the anointing oil and sweet incense","Oil for cooking, and spices for the feasts","Oil for the lamps of the camp, and spices for burial","Oil for healing, and spices for perfume"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 35:8",verse:"And oil for the light, and spices for anointing oil, and for the sweet incense,",insight:"Light, anointing, and incense: the offerings picture a life that shines, is set apart, and prays."},
{q:"Which stones were named among the materials?",options:["Onyx stones, and stones to be set for the ephod and breastplate","Diamonds and rubies for the crown","Marble for the altar base","Flint for the knives"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 35:9",verse:"And onyx stones, and stones to be set for the ephod, and for the breastplate.",insight:"Precious stones were set apart for the high priest's garments. What is closest to God's heart is marked with beauty."},
{q:"Who was to come and make all that the LORD commanded?",options:["Every wise hearted among you","The sons of Aaron only","The strongest of the men","The scribes and the elders"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 35:10",verse:"And every wise hearted among you shall come, and make all that the LORD hath commanded;",insight:"Wise hearted joins skill and devotion. God calls the skillful, and He calls them to bring their hearts too."},
{q:"What moved the people to bring their offerings?",options:["Every one whose heart stirred him up, and whom his spirit made willing","A command with a set amount","Fear of Moses' anger","The promise of double return"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 35:21",verse:"And they came, every one whose heart stirred him up, and every one whom his spirit made willing, and they brought the LORD’S offering to the work of the tabernacle of the congregation, and for all his service, and for the holy garments.",insight:"Stirred hearts, not pressed purses. God moves the giver from within; pressure from without is not His way."},
{q:"What gold jewelry did the people bring?",options:["Bracelets, earrings, rings, and tablets of gold","Crowns and scepters","Chains and anklets of silver","Brooches set with pearls"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 35:22",verse:"And they came, both men and women, as many as were willing hearted, and brought bracelets, and earrings, and rings, and tablets, all jewels of gold: and every man that offered offered an offering of gold unto the LORD.",insight:"The very earrings that once fed the calf now built the tabernacle. Repentance redirects the same gold to a better altar."},
{q:"What did the wise hearted women do?",options:["They spun with their hands what they had","They wove the curtains alone","They sewed the priests' garments","They dyed the threads in the river"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 35:25",verse:"And all the women that were wise hearted did spin with their hands, and brought that which they had spun, both of blue, and of purple, and of scarlet, and of fine linen.",insight:"Women's hands spun the threads of God's house. No skill is too domestic to be woven into worship."},
{q:"What did the women whose hearts stirred them spin?",options:["Goats' hair","Fine linen","Scarlet thread","Blue yarn"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 35:26",verse:"And all the women whose heart stirred them up in wisdom spun goats’ hair.",insight:"Even goats' hair, coarse stuff, was spun in wisdom. God accepts the humble material when the heart is willing."},
{q:"How is the giving of Israel described in Exodus 35:29?",options:["Every man and woman whose heart made them willing brought a willing offering","Only the rich gave, and the poor watched","The Levites collected a fixed tax","Moses commanded and they obeyed"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 35:29",verse:"The children of Israel brought a willing offering unto the LORD, every man and woman, whose heart made them willing to bring for all manner of work, which the LORD had commanded to be made by the hand of Moses.",insight:"Every man and woman gave, each heart willing. Generosity in God's house is everybody's business."},
{q:"Whom did God call by name to lead the work?",options:["Bezalel the son of Uri, of the tribe of Judah","Aholiab the son of Ahisamach, of the tribe of Dan","Moses the son of Amram, of the tribe of Levi","Aaron the priest"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 35:30",verse:"And Moses said unto the children of Israel, See, the LORD hath called by name Bezaleel the son of Uri, the son of Hur, of the tribe of Judah;",insight:"The call is repeated as the work begins. God confirms His chosen leaders when the moment to build arrives."},
{q:"What did God put in Bezalel's heart besides skill?",options:["That he may teach, and Aholiab with him","That he may rule over the workers","That he may judge the tribes","That he may prophesy to Israel"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 35:34",verse:"And he hath put in his heart that he may teach, both he, and Aholiab, the son of Ahisamach, of the tribe of Dan.",insight:"Skill that cannot teach dies with the craftsman. God gave Bezalel the gift of multiplying what he knew."},
{q:"With what were Bezalel and Aholiab filled?",options:["Wisdom of heart, to work all manner of work","Strength of arm for heavy labor","Riches for the building","Favor with the rulers"],a:0,ref:"Exodus 35:35",verse:"Them hath he filled with wisdom of heart, to work all manner of work, of the engraver, and of the cunning workman, and of the embroiderer, in blue, and in purple, in scarlet, and in fine linen, and of the weaver, even of them that do any work, and of those that devise cunning work.",insight:"Wisdom of heart was the final gift named. In God's work, the heart's wisdom outranks the hand's strength."}
]}
]);
